# Conventional Commits

When creating a git commit, use:

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>
```

## Types for this repo

- `test`: new or updated tests, page objects, fixtures
- `fix`: bug fix in tests or config
- `feat`: new coverage, tooling, or workflow
- `refactor`: structure change with no behavior change
- `ci`: GitHub Actions / Playwright CI config
- `docs`: README or comments
- `chore`: deps, ignore files, housekeeping

## Style

- Imperative, lowercase description, no trailing period
- Scope optional: `test(login):`, `ci(playwright):`
- Explain why in the body only when the subject is not enough

```
test(login): cover invalid credentials path

Add a mocked 401 case so the error banner is asserted independently of the API.
```
